\f1\b \cf3 How to use:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
Put this script in your iTunes Scripts folder. This is located in \cf4 home > Library > iTunes\cf0 . If there is no folder named "Scripts" there, create one and put the script in it. It will then appear in iTunes' Script Menu, where you can select it by clicking on its name.\
\
This script is a self-contained AppleScript application\'d0or 
\f2\i applet
\f0\i0 \'d0that can be placed anywhere on your computer and activated by double-clicking its icon. However it is probably most easily accessed from the iTunes Script me\cf2 nu.\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li560\fi-20\ql\qnatural
\cf2 \'a5 This s\cf0 cript reads the "iTunes Music Library.xml" file located in your 
\f2\i \cf4 home > Music > iTunes
\f0\i0 \cf0  folder. iTunes updates this file whenever it is quit. To make sure that everything is up-to-date, you may want to quit and then re-start iTunes before running the script.\
\
(Also, if you have re-located this folder, see "Customizing" below for pointers on editing the script.)\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\cf0 \
\
Run the script, either be selecting it in the iTunes Script menu or by double-clicking on it in the Finder. Select the criteria which you want to use to determine duplicate tracks:\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\cf0 {{\NeXTGraphic Pasted Graphic 1.tiff \width4960 \height4120
}¬}\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\cf0 \
\
Remember that the more criteria you select, the more refined your search will be. On the other hand, just selecting "Artist" and "Bit Rate", for example, will probably just be a waste of your time.\
\
After a 
\f2\i few moments
\f0\i0  you will be notified if any duplicate tracks were discovered. If so, they will be copied to a newly created playlist called "Dupes". This is perhaps the part of the operation that takes the longest. So that you can see that progress is being made, the "Dupes" playlist is selected in iTunes and you will be able to see it filling up with tracks.\
\
If iTunes is the frontmost application when the job is done, a dialog box will tell you the script is finished and the applet will quit. Otherwise, the applet quits silently.\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf3 Stopping Operation:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
If you feel the script is taking too much time, you can select its icon in the Dock, making it the frontmost application, and then press 
\f1\b Command-period
\f0\b0 . This will abort the script. You can always run it another time.\
\

\f1\b \cf3 Customizing:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
There are a few things you can add to or change about the script. \
\
Open the script in Script Editor by using Script Editor's "Open..." command in the File menu. Look for this section of code near the top of the script:\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

